Fox-1D, AO-92 or AMSAT OSCAR 92 was an American amateur radio satellite. Fox-1D was a 1U CubeSat developed and built by AMSAT-NA. Fox-1D carried a single-channel transponder for mode U/V in FM. Fox-1D had an L-band converter, which allowed the FM transponder to be switched on an uplink in the 23 centimetres (9.1 in) band. To enable it to launch under NASA's ELaNa program, the satellite continued to carry the following scientific and technical payloads:
  - High Energy Radiation CubeSat (HERCI);
  - Camera Experiment;
  - MEMS GYRO Experiment. The satellite had a single whip antenna for the 70 cm and 23 cm bands (uplink), as well as an antenna for the 2 m band (downlink).

